/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 326 0 R
/T (This flowchart outlines our autonomous pathing strategy for handling different motifs. The process begins by identifying the start point and scanning the assigned motif. From there, two possible starting conditions are evaluated: goal start pose and far start pose. Regardless of the starting condition, both paths converge on a unified solution: turning the turret toward the goal and scoring the artifact. The specific outcomes and pathing adjustments vary depending on the three distinct motif types. Each motif introduces unique routing considerations and scoring behaviors, which will be detailed in the following sections.)
/E (This flowchart outlines our autonomous pathing strategy for handling different motifs. The process begins by identifying the start point and scanning the assigned motif. From there, two possible starting conditions are evaluated: goal start pose and far start pose. Regardless of the starting condition, both paths converge on a unified solution: turning the turret toward the goal and scoring the artifact. The specific outcomes and pathing adjustments vary depending on the three distinct motif types. Each motif introduces unique routing considerations and scoring behaviors, which will be detailed in the following sections.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [19]
>>
