/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 2420 0 R
/T (Positive bearing: A positive bearing indicates the AprilTag is to the right of the camera's center. The PID output will be a positive value, telling the robot to turn clockwise. Our code sets the motors to turn the robot to the right: frontLeft.setTargetPosition\(-turnPosition\), frontRight.setTargetPosition\(turnPosition\), and so on.)
/E (Positive bearing: A positive bearing indicates the AprilTag is to the right of the camera's center. The PID output will be a positive value, telling the robot to turn clockwise. Our code sets the motors to turn the robot to the right: frontLeft.setTargetPosition\(-turnPosition\), frontRight.setTargetPosition\(turnPosition\), and so on.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 2421 0 R
/T (Negative bearing: A negative bearing means the tag is to the left. The PID output will be negative, and the robot will turn counter-clockwise.)
/E (Negative bearing: A negative bearing means the tag is to the left. The PID output will be negative, and the robot will turn counter-clockwise.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
